/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 98 0 R
/T (Every musician should start their practice session by playing complete free: no rules, no limits, no judgment. Just throw your hands on your instrument and see what comes out of it. Try to push the boundaries, play atonal chords, clusters, angular melodies, extended techniques, unusual constrats. Your ears may complain, and your brain may start judging \("this is bull****"\). Try to overcome these initial impulses. I recommend playing free for around 10 mins. )
/E (Every musician should start their practice session by playing complete free: no rules, no limits, no judgment. Just throw your hands on your instrument and see what comes out of it. Try to push the boundaries, play atonal chords, clusters, angular melodies, extended techniques, unusual constrats. Your ears may complain, and your brain may start judging \("this is bull****"\). Try to overcome these initial impulses. I recommend playing free for around 10 mins. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
