/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 99 0 R
/T (The piece has no melody, just a sequence of 5 different modes over which each improviser takes a solo. Notice how Miles starts his solo by emphasizing the note G, and repeating 4 times a musical gesture that ends on G. On the last time, he gracefully ends on A to signify a conclusion of his first statement. Listen to the recording, and notice how simple it is. )
/E (The piece has no melody, just a sequence of 5 different modes over which each improviser takes a solo. Notice how Miles starts his solo by emphasizing the note G, and repeating 4 times a musical gesture that ends on G. On the last time, he gracefully ends on A to signify a conclusion of his first statement. Listen to the recording, and notice how simple it is. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
