/Title (I like to think about these as the natural stages of evolution of any creative idea \(regardless of the field\). A creative idea starts as humor \(a joke, a parody, a riddle, a mistake\), which then evolves into science \(understanding the reasons, the theory behind the initial idea\), and eventually becoming art \(the process isn't rational anymore, it's purely expressive/poetic\).)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 434 0 R
/Prev 492 0 R
/Next 493 0 R
>>
endobj
543 0 obj
<<
/Title (Every musician should start their practice session by playing complete free: no rules, no limits, no judgment. Just throw your hands on your instrument and see what comes out of it. Try to push the boundaries, play atonal chords, clusters, angular melodies, extended techniques, unusual constrats. Your ears may complain, and your brain may start judging \("this is bull****"\). Try to overcome these initial impulses. I recommend playing free for around 10 mins.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 494 0 R
/Next 566 0 R
>>
endobj
